{#
  The to-hit Section: a table per category, rather than a heading per rule. A
  modifier is one line of data — name, two numbers, a condition — so prose
  headings would bury the comparison the reader actually came for.

  The note column only appears when some row in the group fills it: an empty
  column reads as missing data rather than as nothing to say.
#}
{%- for group in section.body.groups %}
### {{ group.title }}

{% if group.has_notes -%}
| Modifier | To hit | To be hit | Note |
| -------- | ------ | --------- | ---- |
{% for row in group.rows -%}
| {{ row.name }} | {{ row.to_hit }} | {{ row.to_be_hit }} | {{ row.note or "" }} |
{% endfor -%}
{%- else -%}
| Modifier | To hit | To be hit |
| -------- | ------ | --------- |
{% for row in group.rows -%}
| {{ row.name }} | {{ row.to_hit }} | {{ row.to_be_hit }} |
{% endfor -%}
{%- endif -%}
{% endfor -%}
